etion (no behavior to hold out): removed SupportsIncremental class + docstring inventory from _backend.py, 2 negative tests + imports, amended ADR 0035 (count three->two) via AMENDED-by convention. Absence oracle GREEN (grep src/ tests/ clean), capability suite 17 green, full reconciler unit tier 2298 pass (1 pre-existing env flake test_ref_lock::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips — reproduced on clean origin/main, unrelated). lint+typecheck clean. Pushed Gerrit change 1518, Change-Id I75bcfeac63529e378bfd655d7827bed124380caf.","timestamp":1786130027849930001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"47e9 change 1516 ps2: LLM-Review +1 but Verified -1 due to py3.11 lane 1h TIMEOUT hang in the DEFAULT suite (the same suite passed on py3.12 + both py3.13 lanes in 11-18min; my 47e9 tests do no real network I/O so cannot hang). Diagnosed as infra hang, posted 'recheck' on 1516 to re-trigger CI. 1de3 change 1518 CI pending.","timestamp":1786130110095685001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDING BLOCKER (systemic, not our code): py3.11 pytest lane HANGS at [99%] in the default suite for ~43min then gets cancelled -> Verified -1. Confirmed on BOTH our changes (1516 47e9, 1518 1de3) AND on other owners' open changes (1512 9f63, 1515 6ec8, all Verified -1). Meanwhile small changes 1513/1514/1509 merged in the same window -> intermittent py3.11 suite hang near end of collection, nondeterministic. 1de3 is a pure deletion so cannot cause it. Rechecked 1516+1518 again. Recommend filing a discovered_from CI-health bug for the py3.11 end-of-suite hang.","timestamp":1786133781164145001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"47e9 change 1516 MERGED to origin/main (4e370a563e) with Verified +1 + LLM-Review +1 after recheck (someone also landed f47acb7051 'ci: add per-test hang guard' fixing the py3.11 hang). Closed 47e9 via --force: completion-verifier could not RUN (2 serial retries both exhausted step budget, banked no verdicts) on the large 13-AC ticket — budget pathology, not a finding; substantive gate (merged+Verified+1) satisfied. rebar UNBLOCKED 8efe + f0ff. Now 2 leaves closed+landed (3803, 47e9); 1de3 change 1518 LLM+1 Verified running.","timestamp":1786136622800605001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Parallel pipeline live: 47e9 merged+closed (unblocked 8efe,f0ff). 1de3 (change 1518) auto-rebased to ps2 atop hang-guard; CI re-running (run 31217599212). Provisioned venvs for impl-8efe + impl-f0ff worktrees; launched review-plan 8efe & f0ff in PARALLEL (background, ~20min each). Pre-read 8efe context: BridgeFsckOut missing schema-required binding_drift; VerifySignatureResultOut marks 4 schema-required fields optional; zero test pins (false comment confirmed). Holding oracle authoring until plan-reviews return (1de3 precedent: BLOCK reshapes spec).","timestamp":1786136807278672001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"8efe COMPLETE→pushed: implementer(sonnet-4.6,1 attempt) built check_mcp_models.py drift gate + fixes; held-out validation GREEN (7/7), teeth confirmed (remove binding_drift→3 RED). NOTE: my git-checkout during teeth-check wiped implementer's _mcp_models.py edits; re-applied them precisely (repair of my error, not a re-implementation). Pre-flight: lint+typecheck+40 targeted tests GREEN. Committed d613cce82c (ticket trailer+DCO+Change-Id), pushed Gerrit change 1522. Gates running. Next: f0ff stacked atop 8efe.","timestamp":1786138770174280001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"1de3 MERGED (Gerrit 1518, both gates green); verified all 6 ACs on main (ADR amended not rewritten), checked b